Day 1 — Port Stage A and Stage B as-is, wrap them, run 1 tiny end-to-end locally
Deliverables

Orchestra/stageA_builder/ contains the old builder code, runnable in-place

Orchestra/stageB_simulator/local/ contains the old local sim runner, runnable

One ligand from SMILES → build → tiny sim → archived somewhere → visible via Stage C view

run_manifest.json emitted

Steps

Copy, don’t refactor

Put your existing builder repo/scripts into:

Orchestra/stageA_builder/src/ (plus env/requirements if needed)

Put your existing simulator runner scripts into:

Orchestra/stageB_simulator/local/src/

Orchestra/stageB_simulator/templates/ for mdin templates

Decide the “build output format”

One ligand build creates:

builds/<ligand_norm>/ containing system.prmtop, system.inpcrd, ligand files, plus run_manifest.json template.

Define a local run working dir

stageB_simulator/local/work/<ligand_norm>/<rep>/

B copies in build artifacts, runs, writes outputs, writes/updates run_manifest.json.

Archive target (for now)

For Day 1 local test, you can archive to a local “toy archive root” under MSE_LAB:

Orchestra/stageC_archive/pointers/archive_local_test.txt

points to Orchestra/stageC_archive/archive_local_test_root/

This avoids touching WD8 while plumbing is fragile.

Composer rebuild indexes this test archive

Stage C view should show the new test run under views/runs/...

That proves A/B can feed the spine.

You end Day 1 with: “I can run one ligand end-to-end locally, and it appears in Stage C view.”
